Disable Remote Settings and telemetry antifeatures in Abrowser.

Interceptions sit at stable source chokepoints (function entry) and ignore
their arguments.

All disabled functions return the benign empty shape their callers expect
so consumers degrade gracefully instead of throwing.

The Attachments.sys.mjs (base Downloader) cuts were previously applied by sed
in make-firefox (lines 40-42); they are folded in here as a patch.

  services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs         - attachment download (subclass)
  services/settings/Utils.sys.mjs                        - remote settings sync
  services/settings/Attachments.sys.mjs                  - attachment download (base)
  toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetrySend.sys.mjs - ping transport

diff --git a/services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs b/services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs
--- a/services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs
+++ b/services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs
@@ -217,2 +217,7 @@
   async download(record, options) {
+    // Abrowser: attachment download disabled (privacy). Return the empty shape
+    // callers expect ({ buffer }) so ML / translations / search consumers and
+    // ASRouter degrade gracefully instead of throwing on null.
+    console.warn("Function 'download' disabled in Abrowser due to privacy concerns.");
+    return { buffer: new ArrayBuffer(0), record, _source: "disabled" };
     await lazy.UptakeTelemetry.report(

